(library
 ; The port's own library, wrapped: the routing core is [Seekwright.Router] to
 ; its callers (plans/project-structure.md). It depends on [mcp-caps] rather
 ; than the other way round, which is what keeps dropping the capability layer
 ; a seekwright-side change — and today it depends on nothing at all.
 ;
 ; No [libraries] field is deliberate: the routing core stands only on the
 ; standard library, which is what makes it the module a compiled rewrite
 ; implements 1:1. That is checked, not promised, and by two things: this
 ; absence means a reference to [Mcp_caps] or any other out-of-library module
 ; fails the compile, and the [ocamldep] diff in test/dune pins the router's
 ; dependencies inside the library, so reaching for a later seekwright module
 ; fails the runtest alias rather than passing review.
 (name seekwright)
 (public_name seekwright))
